body:
Filed by the triage seat (2026-08-20 round, session `session_016A4EBi3ky1mjTi6vD2kCvA`), relaying a measured platform-fact change out of #10076 (its "⚠️ 立卡时实测到一条与 platform-readings.md:107 相抵触的写侧读数" section) so the fact-table correction has a carrier in the skills lane. `finding` — skills seat self-triages.

The measurement (three writes to one issue body, each read back; full table on #10076):

1. bare HTML-comment-shaped marker → deleted whole, blank line left;
2. the same marker **inside a fenced code block** → still deleted, empty fence left — this is the row that contradicts the fact table, which records "围栏块整体存活(含带尖括号的正则,删感叹号是唯一例外)";
3. bare identifier `os-decision-facets` (no angle brackets) → survives.

Consequences worth carrying into the correction:
- the fact table's "唯一例外" list is missing at least "tag-shaped tokens inside fences (issue bodies)";
- any four-facet block written into an issue BODY with the full comment-shaped marker silently loses its marker (write returns 200) — the mandated write-then-read-back is the only detection; comments are unaffected (markers measured surviving in comments the same day);
- the SKILL's extraction contract (literal-text grep, not comment shape) already tolerates the bare-identifier fallback #10076 used.

The fix is a one-row edit to `.claude/skills/pm-dispatch/references/platform-readings.md` — governed surface, draft PR, human merge.
